An ingest whose next file cannot be created, with no memory to publish the
degraded state, throws std::bad_alloc in the I/O error's place. ingest_rotate
serves both the mid-slice rotation and the one after the last chunk.
Reverts #618.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: ingest whose rotation cannot create a file, refuse writes: ingest's post-loop rotation cannot create a file"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
index 8b83e51..a9a9bf7 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
@@ -230,8 +230,8 @@ void DB::ingest_rotate(TransientEngineState &t,
   try {
     rotation = prepare_rotation(t);
   } catch (...) {
-    degrade_from(current,
-                 "ingest post-rotation file creation failed: call resume().");
+    store_state(current->degraded_copy(
+        "ingest post-rotation file creation failed: call resume()."));
     throw;
   }
   finish_rotation(t, std::move(rotation));
